# BIGQUERY SCHEMA CONFIGURATION
# Switches between different client BigQuery schemas
# Available options: 'default', 'CMF'
#
# Usage:
# - 'default': Generic e-commerce schema for testing/development
# - 'CMF': Cooperativa de Ahorro y Crédito (Alba MCP, localhost:8081)
#
# Change this value to switch between clients:
BIGQUERY_CLIENT_SCHEMA=CMF

# NOTES:
# - Changes take effect on next Node.js process restart
# - NO code changes required to switch schemas
# - Each schema has its own MCP routing (bigquery_intelligence vs. alba)
# - Phase 3.2 tests will continue to work with 'default' schema
# - CMF pilot testing requires 'CMF' schema + Alba MCP running on localhost:8081

# ============================================================================
# CMF-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION (when BIGQUERY_CLIENT_SCHEMA=CMF)
# ============================================================================
# Alba MCP endpoint: http://localhost:8081/alba/intelligent-query
# BigQuery project: chz-bi-cmf-datascience-prod
# Dataset: chz-bi-dwh-prod.CMF_TABLAS_TEMPORALES
# Authentication: Service Account (GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS)
# Main table: VOLCAN_TCMOV (694M+ transactions)

# ============================================================================
# ROLLBACK INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================================================
# To revert to Phase 3.1/3.2 behavior:
# 1. Change BIGQUERY_CLIENT_SCHEMA=default
# 2. Restart Node.js process
# 3. All Phase 3.2 tests should pass
